## Summary

- `datagrid()` builds the covariate product; each row is one `unit` in `InterpretResult`.
- Interventional curves use `set={...}`; associational baselines omit it (`causal=False`).
- On a Bernoulli outcome the response scale is probability, not log-odds.
- Structural and adjustment estimators share the API; overlay them when teaching the two paths.

**Next steps:** [Interventional Contrasts](comparisons.qmd) for `diff` / `ratio` / `lift`; [Local Slopes](slopes.qmd) when the effect of ad spend depends on income; [Predictions, Comparisons, and Slopes](../../../user-guide/predictions-comparisons-slopes.qmd) for the contract; [Causal Inference](../../../user-guide/causal-inference.qmd) for `ate()`.

::: {.callout-note}

